    {
      "id": "174597c7-4ee7-4b98-af44-ad8d1856d0f6",
      "notes": "Satiric Emulation\n\nFrog Fractions throws players for a loop when it sheds its math game facade, and after that it never stops changing. The gameplay becomes a parade of genres: preserving somewhat their identity, but playing with the tropes to the delight of old fans, and adding enough basic humor to amuse the unfamiliar. Nothing lingers too long to grow stale, even the game itself. Frog Fractions serves as a refreshing contrast to the tired patterns of flash gaming, not only in its variety, but its capacity to genuinely surprise you with what comes next.\n\n(Written by Man Son You.)"
